        "text_Hby3Ph": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "enlarge_text": false,
            "text": "<p>For twenty-five years I was a primary school teacher, and I loved every one of them. Every school holidays, my husband and I drove to Waihi Beach — and the moment those dunes came into view, something in me exhaled.</p><p>Eight years ago, after my last class, a small boutique came up for lease near that same beach. My husband Tom looked at me across the kitchen table and didn't say a word. He didn't have to.</p><p>I'd spent twenty-five years helping children discover confidence. Now I wanted to help women rediscover theirs. We moved, and that same year I opened the door of Wendy's Waihi Beach for the very first time.</p><p>Now I'm sixty-four, and it's time to close this chapter. Not because something went wrong. Because something went beautifully right — and I'm wise enough to know when a story has reached its ending.</p><p>This is my favourite sale. Every piece I ever chose for this boutique was chosen with one woman in mind — the real one, not the one on the hanger. That hasn't changed.</p><p>Everything must go, at the lowest prices I've ever offered.</p><p>Find something that makes you stop. Trust that feeling. I built this place around exactly that moment.</p><p>With love,<br/>Wendy Anderson<br/>Wendy's Waihi Beach ❤️</p>"
          }
        }
      },
